course: dictionary
lesson: 365
title: Turning the other way
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Anticlockwise means turning in the opposite direction to the hands of a clock. Picture a clock face: the hand moves from 12 to 3, 6, then 9 when it turns clockwise. Anticlockwise goes the other way: from 12 towards 9, then 6, then 3.
explain: You can use it as a describing word too, as in «an anticlockwise turn». Many lids and taps turn anticlockwise to open, so the next time you open a jar, notice which way your hand moves.
explain: Shepherds use calls to guide their dogs and flock over hills. «Come by» means clockwise round the flock, and «away to me» means anticlockwise. The context shows you the direction, even if you have never heard the calls before.
fact: Anticlockwise means turning in the opposite direction to the hands of a clock.
fact: In the US and Canada, people say «counterclockwise» for the same direction.
fact: «Anticlockwise» can describe a turn, as in «an anticlockwise turn».
fact: Huge ocean currents called gyres turn clockwise in the northern hemisphere and anticlockwise in the southern hemisphere.
fact: In PE and dance, children often move round the circle anticlockwise.
exercise: Mia turns the tap «anticlockwise» to open it. Which way does she turn it? | Only a quarter of the way | Round the same way as a clock's hands | *The opposite way to a clock's hands | Straight up and down
exercise: A clock hand moves from 12 to 9. Which way is that? | Up and down | It is not a turn at all | Clockwise | *Anticlockwise
exercise: In the shepherd's calls, which call means anticlockwise round the flock? | «stop» | «come in» | *«away to me» | «come by»
test: The gyres in the southern hemisphere turn which way? | They do not turn | Clockwise | *Anticlockwise | Up and down
test: Which word is the American word for anticlockwise? | *Counterclockwise | Backwise | Clockwise | Anticlock
exam: Which of these is an anticlockwise turn? | 12 to 3, then 6 | *12 to 9, then 6 | Up and down | 6 to 9, then 12
